   - `e_007401` – “The dog eats the rabbit.”  
   - `e_0049cd` – “The cow eats the rabbit.”  
   - `e_00042b` – “The bear eats the rabbit.”  

   Any of these satisfy P, but we select the **first** one encountered that meets the condition: `e_007401`.

3. **Map the conclusion Q** (“the rabbit is round”) to a candidate item.  
   The statement that directly says the rabbit is round is:
   - `e_002cc7` – “The rabbit is round.”  

   This candidate satisfies Q. (All other facts about the rabbit’s roundness do not exist, so we pick `e_002cc7`.)

